    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0082" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg70"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/677: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-17T23:00:00+01:00">December 17, 1942—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 17—8:09 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7149. Department’s telegram 6372, December 16, 8 p.m. Eden tells me that it is
                    unfortunately too late to make the insertion desired by the Department. He says
                    that the text has been agreed upon by Moscow and by the Allied Governments and
                    that it would be impossible to clear the change before the agreed time of
                    release. He also says the wording follows the usual form.<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d68-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
